op of a long page**·A back-to-top control is useful after substantial scrolling, especially when important navigation sits at the top. Keep it out of the way and reveal it only after the user has moved far enough. It does not solve a poorly structured page.\n\nBackTop\n\n## You can say this to an AI Agent\n\n> “\n> Show a Back to top button after the product list scrolls beyond one screen and return users to the filter area. Avoid support and bottom purchase actions, hide it on short pages, and test mobile safe areas, keyboard focus, and reduced motion.\n\n### When to use it\n\n- Long article\n\n↑\n- Long catalog or feed\n\nAll states\n↑\n- Documentation page\n\n↑\n- A page whose main controls are at the top\n\n↑Appears after you scroll far enough\n\n### When NOT to use it\n\n- Show it before the user scrolls\n- Use it on a short page\n\nSubmit↑\n- Cover mobile content or another floating action\n\n↑\n- Treat it as a replacement for clear navigation and sections\n\n☰?\n\nAnatomy\n\n↑\n\n1ViewportThe button appears after the reader scrolls down the page\n\n2FloatButtonFix it in the lower-right corner; clicking scrolls smoothly to the top\n\n3IconUse a clear upward arrow; add text when the meaning is unclear\n\nVariants\n\nCircle\n\n↑\n\nA compact default for standard pages\n\nSquare\n\n↑\n\nWhen the interface has a strong visual style, match its other buttons\n\nWith Text\n\n↑ top\n\nWhen you need to clearly explain what a button does\n\nTypical use cases\n\nLong article\n\n🎧\n\n          \nNoise Canceling Headphones Pro\n\n          \n¥ 899\n\n        \n🎒\n\n          \nOutdoor backpack\n\n          \n¥ 239\n\n      ↑\n\nProduct catalog\n\n**Mountain Life: Weekend Hiking Equipment Checklist**\n      \nRead 3.2k · About 8 minutes\n\n      \n      \n      \n      ↑\n\nDocumentation\n\n↑\n\nActivity feed\n\nQuick start\n        Installation\n        Component\n        Update log\n\n      \n**Quick Start**\n\n      ↑\n\nRecommended tool\n[Web fine-tuning tool · Selector